  "content": "REST handlers follow GOTTH-style DI: one handler per file under internal/handlers/ (getstatus.go, postretry.go, getmemories.go, etc.). Each handler is a struct with a NewXHandlerParams constructor and a ServeHTTP method. Constructor takes the smallest interface that satisfies it (consumer-defined interfaces in deps.go: StatusService, ConfigService, MemoryReader, MemoryEditor, ProjectLister, GraphReader, MemoryStatsReader, UsageReader, Dreamer, SessionStatsProvider, DreamStatsReader, ProjectOverridesService). *App satisfies all of them. routes.go's Register(mux, RegisterParams) wires everything. No chi router — Go 1.22+ stdlib ServeMux pattern matching is enough.\u003c/content\u003e\n\u003ctags\u003e[\"architecture\", \"api\", \"go\", \"dependency-injection\"]\u003c/tags\u003e",
